#
# One assignment keeps a four-valued consequence, in Sutra
# (twelvefold_rules.h TR2). premise is the value code C produced for the
# conjunction of the premises (lpres_conjoin), conclusion the code of the
# conclusion, in the kernel's numbering: NEITHER 0, TRUE 1, FALSE 2,
# BOTH 3. TRUE and BOTH are designated. The assignment keeps the
# consequence when the premise is not designated or the conclusion is.
# A code past 3 is no value: storing -1 in the unsigned check field is a
# size error, refused; a negative code does not fit 9: refused.
record entail-kept
  premise: 9
  conclusion: 9
  nocode: 9
procedure
  if premise > 3 or conclusion > 3
    compute nocode = 0 - 1
  end-if
  answer premise = 0 or premise = 2 or conclusion = 1 or conclusion = 3
